en:
"They say we're doing a test of courage
at the freshman welcome party.
I'm no good with scary stuff~..."{w}

{0E}"I sense a power hidden within you all!
Yes, you have what it takes to become heroes!{0F}
The makings of heroes who will save this world!"{w}{p}"But that power has not yet awakened!{w}I shall guide you!{w}Down the road that leads to heroism!"{w}

{0E}"To think you would endure every last one of my trials...
From this day forth, you may call yourselves heroes!!{0F}
Nothing could make me happier!!"{w}

"In that case,
I shall pump them full of vigor
so they take on a form worthy of you!"{w}

{0E}"Here I go!
Nnnnnghhhhhhh...{0F}
Bwahahahahaha!!"{w}

"The road you have walked so far
will become new strength
and support you in body and soul!"{w}

"I just don't understand how young people think these days.{w}I give them tougher assignments
thinking it'll help them grow, and they run off."{w}{p}"So then I give them easy stuff instead,
and they just keep getting worse and worse...{w}Hrrrmm..."{w}

"I may have said that, but
being a school teacher is hard...
No tiiiime~......"{w}

A short way off, a mage was muttering
words you couldn't make out.{w}A teacher, perhaps?{w}{p}Soon the mage noticed you, broke into a slimy grin,
hitched up the robe, and came charging straight at you.{w}

"...So, thing is, we've got ourselves a problem.{w}Ogre Bay's had these special cannon blueprints
handed down since way back."{w}{p}"I got 'em from my old man too, but...{w}see, the... blueprints, I kinda... went an' lost 'em...
At this rate, we can't build it!!"{w}
